Resolve the repository root with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`. Create a precise `ChangeLog/` entry describing the intended change and verification.

Audit the intended diff for credentials, personal paths, machine names, hostnames, tailnet identifiers, IP addresses, databases, uploads, environment files, and other private data. Sanitize or exclude every finding.

Run `npm run verify`. Commit only the intended files, push a new branch to the configured `origin`, and open a new draft pull request targeting `main`. Keep unrelated worktree changes out of the commit and provide the pull request URL and verification result.
